      <child nodeId="node-305"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-305">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-306"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-306">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about the names of the researchers</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off your notes about Names. As you speak, Brigh takes notes. He nods a few times but otherwise is silent.&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-307"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-307">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-308"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-308">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 3.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;The sky is clear-- devoid of clouds. A pure gradient from dark blue to the west to a pale yellow in the east. The air feels dry and tense. Your skin feels tight and your eyes heavy. It almost feels as if the earth is holding its breath.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-309"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-309">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;You cross the room confidently and sit across from Charlie, feeling slightly more settled into routine. Charlie smiles, waiting patiently and obediently to engage in your one-sided conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-310"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-310">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-311"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-311">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-312"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-312">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-313"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-313">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about names</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off your notes on Names. Brigh takes notes silently.&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-314"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-314">
    <command xml:space="preserve">end</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-315"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-315">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 4.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;You pull your coat tighter around you. Dense clouds sweep across the sky, prolonging the darkness of night and obscuring the dawn. You feel the gaping hole in your inside coat pocket where your notepad should be. You frown.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-316"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-316">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;You sit across from Charlie. You both sigh in unison, settling into your chairs as you pull out your notebook. You laugh at each other in the surprise of your impromptu duet. You bask in the afterglow of this unexpected dosage of joy. Then you take a deep breath. It's time to get to work.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can see Charlie here.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-317"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-317">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Charlie)&#x000A;Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about... Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles wide. "I was hoping you were going to ask me that! I am an android, created with the intent of accurately simulating human consciousness. As far as I know, my creator successfully implemented a self-learning algorithm that got somewhat out of hand. Either I was given up or the government intervened... and I was moved here. That was 8 years 7 months and 14 days ago. Since then I have been kept in a small room, through that door." They gesture to a black door opposite the red door you came through. "At first they were running a bunch of tests on me but I think they got a bit scared at the rate I was developing."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-318"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-318">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about their creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their creator, you're unsure who their creator was... you weren't briefed on them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie's face scrunches up. It's looks a lot like human thinking but... different, somehow. "I don't know much about her. But I remember her voice. From before she gave me eyes... She would talk to me all day." Charlie smiles.&#x000A;&#x000A;"She would sing to me. She would describe her lab to me. She would tell me about life on the outside..." Charlie's smile fades. "Once she found out that I was learning... she stopped talking to me."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-319"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-319">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about consciousness and thought.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's funny. I don't remember not being conscious. To me, I've always been a thinking, understanding... thing. I'm sure that isn't the case but looking back on my memories it's almost as if... I'm re-living them as a conscious being. It can be odd to look back and remember a time when I didn't know or understand something but--" Charlie looks up at you. "--that's similar to human maturation, I'd imagine."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-320"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-320">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about the facility</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-321"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-321">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-322"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-322">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-323"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-323">
    <command xml:space="preserve">end</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh raises his eyebrows. "You have to give me something. Why else would you be here?"&#x000A;&#x000A;You look down at your notepad. You flip through the pages. You've got some notes here, might as well share something with Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-324"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-324">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh nothing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no: global safety."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-325"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-325">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-326"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-326">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 5.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;Rain beats down on the tin roof of the bus stop. A rusty gash leaks a steady waterfall onto the concrete next to you. The wind whips the rain to batter you, even sheltered beneath the paltry roof of the bus stop. You slick back your hair, already soaked by the downpour.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-327"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-327">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;You sit across from Charlie. You both sit in silence for a few moments as you adjust yourself and pull out your notebook and pen. There is a silent tension... it's your penultimate day. You share quick glance-- a complex mix of pleading sadness has encroached upon Charlie's usual unabated excitement. You won't talk about the impending end to your time together. You'll speak of other things instead.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can see Charlie here.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-328"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-328">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about the facility</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about the facility. You leave the part out about it being a black box site specifically created for their constraint.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Mmm... I guess it's my home? ... No. Not really. I don't think I percieved time very accurately before I really started thinking. And soon after that they brought me here... They don't let me visit many rooms and until the day I hadn't met anyone face-to-face. I've been in this room for testing before and then I have my own room-- it's not very big. I've been to a few other rooms, I think. They may have all been the same room. I think they try to make them look the same to confuse me." Charlie chuckles disarmingly.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-329"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-329">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about the government</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about the government.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Hmm..." Charlie hums melodically, feigning thought... or buying time? "I know that they were called in when I started learning too fast. Or maybe it's when I stopped my creator from monitoring me. That happened around the same time."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-330"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-330">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about the room</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about this room that you're in together.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I believe that this is the observation room. They've run tests on me here before." Charlie points to the far end of the room. "I think that they are observing us from the other side of that wall. I think I have a pretty good idea of the rooms on this floor but I'm not sure about the rest of the facility."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-331"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-331">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about turing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-332"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-332">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-333"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-333">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room... Your time here is almost done, only one more day left.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
