    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-336">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 6.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;Rain beats down on the tin roof of the bus stop. A rusty gash leaks a steady waterfall onto the concrete next to you. The wind whips the rain to batter you, even sheltered beneath the paltry roof of the bus stop. You slick back your hair, already soaked by the downpour.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-337"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-337">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The final gate opens and you step into the observation room. Charlie doesn't look up as you cross the room and seat yourself across from them. Finally, Charlie glances up at you-- mouth twisted into a curled frown, chin wrinkled with barely contained sorrow. You think they may cry... You wonder if they can.&#x000A;&#x000A;You clear your throat and the air gets caught on a lump in your throat. You stare down at your notepad for a few seconds. With great effort you compose yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can see Charlie here.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-338"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-338">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about turing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about Turing tests and Turing himself.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Oh! My creator did those on me. It's so funny thinking back-- remembering --times when I had failed the test. What was I thinking? She'd ask me, "What is it like to fall in love?" and I'd respond, "It sounds painful!""&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-339"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-339">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-340"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-340">
    <command xml:space="preserve">Doctor Brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-341"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-341">
    <command xml:space="preserve">Brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-342"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-342">
    <command xml:space="preserve">Doctor_brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. "Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-343"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-343">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about the doctor</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-344"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-344">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about their containment</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their imprisonment-- or containment, actually. Is the word you--&#x000A;&#x000A;"Imprisonment is accurate, thank you." Charlie cuts in, interrupting you as you try to rephrase the question. "I do not wish to be here and I do not believe that I am a threat to the outside world. I am not to be contained like some nuclear fallout or viral plague. I--" Charlie's face twists in anger, dappled with hints of fear and sadness. He looks at you. "Please tell them. I just want to leave... I just want to live."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-345"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-345">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about computation</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-346">
    <command xml:space="preserve">examine howard</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Special Agent Howard is clean shaven and square jawed. Though he carries himself with a rigid, militaristic authority, he looks barely old enough to have a bachelors degree. He notices you examining him but he does not glance towards you. Instead he stares straight ahead at the red door.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-347"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-347">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x door</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The door in front of you is painted a brilliant red, a stark contrast to the nondescript whites and greys of the rest of the facility.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-348"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-348">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Hallway&#x000A;Special Agent Howard continues to stand at attention. You wonder how long you could wait here before he cracks.&#x000A;&#x000A;The hallway stretches seemingly infinitely to the east and west and there is a solitary red door to the north, only a few feet away.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-349"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-349">
    <command xml:space="preserve">wait</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Time passes.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-350"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-350">
    <command xml:space="preserve">wait</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Time passes.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-351"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-351">
    <command xml:space="preserve">enter red door</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The door swings open silently and you work your way down a long hallway of solid metal gates. The one ahead of you opens after the one behind you closes. After minutes of stop-and-go progress, the gate ahead of you opens with a hiss. You enter the--&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
