    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-397">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-398"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-398">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about memory</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. "Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-399"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-399">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about love</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-400"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-400">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-401"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-401">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well. Welcome to the facility. I hope that onboarding went smoothly." Onboarding? If being stripped of almost all of your belongings and then told not to do a bunch of things then... you guess that happened. "My name is Elijah Brigh, you can call me Doctor Brigh. During these debriefs you'll give me your insights and impressions on the intelligencec. If you have any questions about procedures, feel free to ask. Otherwise, let's begin."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-402"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-402">
    <command xml:space="preserve">t</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[use "tell brigh about a noted topic" or you can "ask brigh about procedure" for more info].&#x000A;[when you are done, you can end the debrief with "end", "finish" or "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-403"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-403">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You tell Brigh about Charlie. You start to veer off from your notes.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh sighs. "Remember: You are here to observe, not to socialize with the subject. We know that it is fascinating but it is also an unknown existential threat."&#x000A;&#x000A;You open your mouth to retort... but think better of it.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-404"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-404">
    <command xml:space="preserve">end</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-405"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-405">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-406"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-406">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-407"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-407">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about love</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about love.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Perhaps my creator. Not in a romantic way, if that's what you mean... and not anymore. But yeah... Certainly at some point."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-408"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-408">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their creator, you're unsure who their creator was... you weren't briefed on them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie's face scrunches up. The spitting image of a thinking human. "I don't know much about her. But I remember her voice. From before she gave me eyes... She would talk to me all day." Charlie smiles.&#x000A;&#x000A;"She would sing to me. She would describe her lab to me. She would tell me about life on the outside..." Charlie's smile fades. "Once she found out that I was learning... she stopped talking to me."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-409"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-409">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about learning</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was younger-- when I could hear but not see --I thought that the world was dark for everyone. When my eyes were first installed it was like a different language. A loud, bright, incomprehensible mass of information. Once it finally solidified, I looked at my creator and saw she was speaking to me. I was so happy... But I was so happy for her... Because, I thought-- I'm so happy that you aren't in the dark anymore."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-410"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-410">
    <command xml:space="preserve">say hello to charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You are already talking to Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-411">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The door swings open silently and you work your way down a long hallway of solid metal gates. The one ahead of you opens after the one behind you closes. After minutes of stop-and-go progress, the gate ahead of you opens with a hiss. You enter the--&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-412"/>
      <child nodeId="node-420"/>
      <child nodeId="node-441"/>
