    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-412">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about body</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about their vessel, the body that they exist in.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I have lived in many bodies throughout my life, so I can't imagine that I am as precious about it as you might be-- or as a human might be, I mean. My body hasn't been updated since my first year here when they did the most work on me, before they started prohibiting interaction. I got new skin and higher fidelity limbs." Charlie raises their right hand, turning it over and inspecting it. "It's a strange thing, a body."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-413"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-413">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-414"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-414">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about death</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about death and its inevitability: the concept of mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't age... but I feel that some day I will die..." Charlie pauses. They look up at the ceiling, thinking for a moment. "But I like for things to end... Not in a mean way. It just wouldn't be so special unless at some point, quite tragically, it wasn't."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-415"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-415">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken notes on the subjects of their body, life and mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;You could try to follow up on some of these, perhaps Charlie has more to say.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-416"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-416">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on life.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie considers themself to be alive and bases this consideration in their perception of being through memory. I find this hard to argue as I am no different."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about mortality, religion and consciousness. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-417"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-417">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on mortality</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie understands mortality and seems to even believe it to be inevitable for them. They are melancholic in their description of death but oddly hopeful in their musings about the meaning imbued by the impermanence of life."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about life, grief and violence. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-418"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-418">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on body</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on body.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-419"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-419">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on their body</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on their body.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie acknowledges what should be a disconnect between their consciousness and body. I sense a sliver of doubt in Charlie's supposed separation from their body."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about *** Couldn't read from entry 30 of a list which has entries numbered from 1 to 29 ***&#x000A;&#x000A;*** Run-time problem P50: Attempt to use list item which does not exist.&#x000A;&#x000A;life, grief and violence. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-420">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know that they are the principal investigator in this facility... I still remember the first thing they said to me--" Charlie puts on a faux frown and speaks in a gruff voice. "No Turings for you Charlie. I know you'd pass. No point in doin" that." The impression takes you so by surprise that you can't help but laugh. It's actually quite a good impression. You're sure that Charlie would be capable of perfectly recreating the Doctor's voice... but they elected instead to create a caricatured, flawed impersonation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-421"/>
      <child nodeId="node-426"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-421">
    <command xml:space="preserve"></command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I beg your pardon?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-422"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-422">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken a note on the subject of doctor brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-423"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-423">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-424"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-424">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on doctor brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie knows about Doctor Brigh individually and that he is the principal investigator of the facility. This was to be expected." Scribbled in the margins, next to this note is a small passage that reads, "Charlie doees quite a good impression of Brigh. I'm sure that Charlie would be capable of perfectly recreating the Doctor's voice... but they elected instead to create a flawed impersonation that captured Brigh's character. I wonder if he'd be flattered."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about the researchers, turing and the facility. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-425"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-425">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about me</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Myself)&#x000A;You ask Charlie about yourself. What had they told Charlie?&#x000A;&#x000A;"About you? Absolutely nothing. They told me that someone was going to come study me. I half expected a mannequin with a built-in microphone. I know you're not supposed to tell me things but... well... I wish I did know more about you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-426">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. "Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-427"/>
      <child nodeId="node-432"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-427">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken a note on the subject of doctor brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-428"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-428">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about surveillance</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about being surveilled.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie chuckles. "They didn't tell you?" You shrug. You don't understand.&#x000A;&#x000A;"They aren't watching. They don't allow any tech to be anywhere near me. They think I might chirp some binary to a microphone and turn the computers against them. Or crash the stock market by signing to a camera... So, yeah. It's just us, for now. No surveillance."&#x000A;&#x000A;You almost don't know what to say. You can't believe that they wouldn't tell-- ... No. you can absolutely imagine these people lying to you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-429"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-429">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on surveillance</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on surveillance.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... It should come as no surprise that aspects of this study have been kept for you." There is a short list neatly formatted beneath this note, it lists:&#x000A;"Things Not Told To Me:"&#x000A;- Charlie is well past a Turing evaluation&#x000A;- the feds think Charlie could kill me&#x000A;- the feds are deathly afraid of Charlie&#x000A;- so much so, they do not even surveil them&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about the researchers, their containment and freedom.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-430"/>
    </children>
  </item>
