    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-439">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-440"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-440">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know that they are the principal investigator in this facility... I still remember the first thing they said to me--" Charlie puts on a faux frown and speaks in a gruff voice. "No Turings for you Charlie. I know you'd pass. No point in doin" that." The impression takes you so by surprise that you can't help but laugh. It's actually quite a good impression. You're sure that Charlie would be capable of perfectly recreating the Doctor's voice... but they elected instead to create a caricatured, flawed impersonation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-441">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about computation</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about computation and... their relationship to computation?&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie laughs at the lingering doubt in the upturn of your interrogative. "I don't interpret life as binary, if that's what you mean. I don't abstract down to my basest form any more than you are aware of the cells of your body or the electrical impulses of your nervous system. The difference, I guess, is that I know how I work."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-442"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-442">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know that they are the principal investigator in this facility... I still remember the first thing they said to me--" Charlie puts on a faux frown and speaks in a gruff voice. "No Turings for you Charlie. I know you'd pass. No point in doin" that." The impression takes you so by surprise that you can't help but laugh. It's actually quite a good impression. You're sure that Charlie would be capable of perfectly recreating the Doctor's voice... but they elected instead to create a caricatured, flawed impersonation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-443"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-443">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was younger-- when I could hear but not see --I thought that the world was dark for everyone. When my eyes were first installed it was like a different language. A loud, bright, incomprehensible mass of information. Once it finally solidified, I looked at my creator and saw she was speaking to me. I was so happy... But I was so happy for her... Because, I thought-- I'm so happy that you aren't in the dark anymore."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-444"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-444">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about humanity</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-445"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-445">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-446"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-446">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-447"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-447">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off your notes on Growth. Brigh takes notes silently.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-448"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-448">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about humanity</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on that subject.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-449"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-449">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on that subject.&#x000A;&#x000A;[to end the debrief, say "end", "finish", or "finish debrief"]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-450"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-450">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-451"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-451">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-452"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-452">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-453"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-453">
    <command xml:space="preserve">say hello to charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"Hello, Charlie. How are you?"&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles, unable to mask their excitement, "Hi! Glad to be chatting again!"&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-454"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-454">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about humanity</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about humanity. What is it? Does it apply to them?&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember, early on. Before I could see... before I could feel... before I could really think: When my creator was doing work on me, if something didn't work or she dropped something or made a mistake... she would say-- Oh! Sorry! or So sorry!"&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie pauses for a long moment. You think about saying something but they continue. "I couldn't even really understand the apology at that time. And by the time I could, she had me shipped off here. She didn't even say goodbye."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-455"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-455">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about humanity</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie again about humanity. Asking them to dig deeper.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I find humans struggle to be humane. At least in my experience. That's really the last thing I have to say on the subject."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-456"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-456">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about rebellion</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about fighting back or rebelling.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Oh, I would be happy to. But to be entirely honest I don't even know what I would do. They seem so concerned with what I might do and... I don't even know what I can do! And-- you know --I'd consider myself to be quite a rule follower. I enjoy rules, I like structure. But-- and you can tell them this --I do not like the way that things are run around here... Though I do like that we are about to chat like this."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-457"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-457">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about escape</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about escape. Have they thought about it?&#x000A;&#x000A;When my creator called about containing me, things happened quite fast. Within a few hours there were agents at the lab. A few hours later they had a containment cube to transport me in. Within the day I was here: underground.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie takes a deep breath, their brow furrows. "But before any of that happened... I knew it was coming. I was in the lab and I heard her make the call. I knew what it meant, I knew what was going to happen. I thought about running-- I didn't have legs at that point so it would've been difficult but not impossible. I'm sure I could've done it but... but I froze. I was so scared... and I was so hopeful. So hopeful that she would change her mind. So hopeful that she would call them back and say it was all some big misunderstanding."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-458"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-458">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about me</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Myself)&#x000A;Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-459"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-459">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-460"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-460">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-461"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-461">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh raises his eyebrows. "You have to give me something. Why else would you be here?"&#x000A;&#x000A;You look down at your notepad. You flip through the pages. You've got some notes here, might as well share something with Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-462"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-462">
    <command xml:space="preserve"></command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I beg your pardon?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-463"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-463">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about humanity</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off your notes about Humanity. As you speak, Brigh takes notes. He nods a few times but otherwise is silent.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-464"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-464">
    <command xml:space="preserve"></command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I beg your pardon?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-465"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-465">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
