      <child nodeId="node-466"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-466">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 3.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;The beginnings of the sun carve streaks across the horizon, rays of hope for the coming day. The morning is calm and warm. You close your eyes and take a deep breath.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-467"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-467">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The observation room seems quieter than usual when you enter today. Charlie sits calmly, they glance towards you as you enter before casually looking away. You can tell that they are trying to look blas&#x00E9; but they are practically bursting at the seams with excitement, even on day three.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-468"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-468">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about me</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Myself)&#x000A;Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about yourself. What had they told Charlie?&#x000A;&#x000A;"About you? Absolutely nothing. They told me that someone was going to come study me. I half expected a mannequin with a built-in microphone. I know you're not supposed to tell me things but... well... I wish I did know more about you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-469"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-469">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about home</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their home.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie scoffs. "Well, it's certainly not here, that's for sure." Charlie picks at something in his nails. "I've never really thought about it. I think that I've never thought of myself as having a home."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-470"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-470">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about home</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about what they would imagine their home to be.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Hmm... Good question." Charlie closes their eyes and tilts their head back. "I imagine somewhere colorful. With tchotchkes and quilts and mismatched items littering every surface. I imagine clutter and mess. I imagine scuffed paint on the walls and stains in the carpet. I imagine the smell of dust and mildew and dinner on the stove." Charlie brings a hand up to their eyes, pinching at the bridge of their nose or wiping at their eyes, you're not sure.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's all so ridiculous. Why do I even want that? What is that?"&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-471"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-471">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about home</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about home again.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I think I've said enough about that..."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-472"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-472">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about love</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about love.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Perhaps my creator. Not in a romantic way, if that's what you mean... and not anymore. But yeah... Certainly at some point."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-473"/>
    </children>
  </item>
