      <child nodeId="node-479"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-479">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 4.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;The sky is clear-- devoid of clouds. A pure gradient from dark blue to the west to a pale yellow in the east. The air feels dry and tense. Your skin feels tight and your eyes heavy. It almost feels as if the earth is holding its breath.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-480"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-480">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;You cross the room confidently and sit across from Charlie, feeling slightly more settled into routine. Charlie smiles, waiting patiently and obediently to engage in your one-sided conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-481"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-481">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about hate</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about hate.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't think I've ever experienced the emotion... Not yet at least."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-482"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-482">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about vengeance</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about vengeance.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-483">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about freedom</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about freedom, you try to frame the discussion around the right itself, not Charlie's specific freedom but--&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was being transported to the facility, I was already at a stage where they feared plugging directly into me, for fear I might... I don't know-- escape? Take over?" Charlie waves their hands dismissively.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, they transported me in a sound-proof metal cube. Correct me if I'm wrong-- I don't believe that humans are transported in that way."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-484"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-484">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about body</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their vessel, the body that they exist in.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I have lived in many bodies throughout my life, so I can't imagine that I am as precious about it as you might be-- or as a human might be, I mean. My body hasn't been updated since my first year here when they did the most work on me, before they started prohibiting interaction. I got new skin and higher fidelity limbs." Charlie raises their right hand, turning it over and inspecting it. "It's a strange thing, a body."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-485"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-485">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about escape</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about escape. Have they thought about it?&#x000A;&#x000A;When my creator called about containing me, things happened quite fast. Within a few hours there were agents at the lab. A few hours later they had a containment cube to transport me in. Within the day I was here: trapped underground.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie takes a deep breath, their brow furrows. "But before any of that happened... I knew it was coming. I was in the lab and I heard her make the call. I knew what it meant, I knew what was going to happen. I thought about running-- I didn't have legs at that point so it would've been difficult but not impossible. I'm sure I could've done it but... but I froze. I was so scared... and I was so hopeful. So hopeful that she would change her mind. So hopeful that she would call them back and say it was all some big misunderstanding."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-486"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-486">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about containment</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-487"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-487">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-488"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-488">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well. Welcome to the facility. I hope that onboarding went smoothly." Onboarding? If being stripped of almost all of your belongings and then told not to do a bunch of things then... you guess that happened. "My name is Elijah Brigh, you can call me Doctor Brigh. During these debriefs you'll give me your insights and impressions on the intelligencec. If you have any questions about procedures, feel free to ask. Otherwise, let's begin."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-489"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-489">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[use "tell brigh about a noted topic" or you can "ask brigh about procedure" for more info].&#x000A;[when you are done, you can end the debrief with "end", "finish" or "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-490"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-490">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken notes on the subjects of freedom, their body and escape.&#x000A;&#x000A;You could try to follow up on some of these, perhaps Charlie has more to say.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-491"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-491">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on freedom</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on freedom.&#x000A;&#x000A;... Charlie is very aware of themselves as a percieved existential threat. They are also very aware of the divide between their treatment and the base right attributed to humans. Regardless of their threat level, it seems to me that the their treatment was and is inhumane and unjust.&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about life, mortality and their containment. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-492"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-492">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on life.&#x000A;&#x000A;[to end the debrief, say "end", "finish", or "finish debrief"]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-493"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-493">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on their body</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on their body.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie acknowledges what should be a disconnect between their consciousness and body. I sense a sliver of doubt in Charlie's supposed separation from their body."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about consciousness, life and mortality. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-494"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-494">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on escape</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on escape.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie reflects on the trauma of their abandonment and how that paralyzed them when offered the possibility of escape. I wonder, if provided with a similar opportunity now, would they attempt to escape?"&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about freedom, rebellion and their containment.  You could also follow up on escape.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-495">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was younger-- when I could hear but not see --I thought that the world was dark for everyone. When my eyes were first installed it was like a different language. A loud, bright, incomprehensible mass of information. Once it finally solidified, I looked at my creator and saw she was speaking to me. I was so happy... But I was so happy for her... Because, I thought-- I'm so happy that you aren't in the dark anymore."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-496"/>
      <child nodeId="node-499"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-496">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie to expand on their thoughts on growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie laughs. "I guess I didn't really answer the question, did I? It's not just that I've grown to understand that everyone else is living lives separate from me... I feel like I am finding my place in existence-- or where I want to be. My purpose.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-497"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-497">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie to continue expanding on the subject of growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Sometimes I imagine what it might be like to... To grow without the constraints of this facility." Charlie trails off, wringing their hands. "I think that would be nice. A good goal, I guess."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-498"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-498">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie still fixates on an external understanding of progression. This is to be expected as the paradigm of their existence is predicated on their access to or censorship from training data (any information that may progress Charlie's learning model)... I find it very hard to write clinically about Charlie, they do not present like the algorithms I have studied in the past."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about life and mortality.  And you could follow up on growth too.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-499">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie still fixates on an external understanding of progression. This is to be expected as the paradigm of their existence is predicated on their access to or censorship from training data (any information that may progress Charlie's learning model)... I find it very hard to write clinically about Charlie, they do not present like the algorithms I have studied in the past."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about life and mortality.  You could also follow up on growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-500"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-500">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken a note on the subject of growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-501"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-501">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-502"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-502">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken notes on the subjects of growth and life.&#x000A;&#x000A;You could try to follow up on some of these, perhaps Charlie has more to say.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-503"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-503">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life again.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I think I've said enough about that..."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-504">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. "Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-505"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-505">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> tell charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-506"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-506">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-507"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-507">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;temp desc&#x000A;&#x000A;Shit! You haven't taken any notes... You'll have to come clean with Doctor Brigh and tell him... nothing.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-508"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-508">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on that subject.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-509"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-509">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about nothing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no: global safety."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-510"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-510">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-511"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-511">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-512"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-512">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-513"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-513">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-514"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-514">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask chahrlie about consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-515"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-515">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about consciousness and thought.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's funny. I don't remember not being conscious. To me, I've always been a thinking, understanding... thing. I'm sure that isn't the case but looking back on my memories it's almost as if... I'm re-living them as a conscious being. It can be odd to look back and remember a time when I didn't know or understand something but--" Charlie looks up at you. "--that's similar to human maturation, I'd imagine."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-516"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-516">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about love</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Love or Hate?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-517"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-517">
    <command xml:space="preserve">love</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Love or Hate?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-518"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-518">
    <command xml:space="preserve">hate</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie frowns. "I don't care to talk about that. It bores me."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-519"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-519">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Charlie)&#x000A;You ask Charlie about... Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles wide. "I was hoping you were going to ask me that! I am an android, created with the intent of accurately simulating human consciousness. As far as I know, my creator successfully implemented a self-learning algorithm that got somewhat out of hand. Either I was given up or the government intervened... and I was moved here. That was 8 years 7 months and 14 days ago. Since then I have been kept in a small room, through that door." They gesture to a black door opposite the red door you came through. "At first they were running a bunch of tests on me but I think they got a bit scared at the rate I was developing."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-520"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-520">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask chharlie about me</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-521"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-521">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about me</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Myself)&#x000A;Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-522"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-522">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
