  <item nodeId="node-529">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 3.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;The beginnings of the sun carve streaks across the horizon, rays of hope for the coming day. The morning is calm and warm. You close your eyes and take a deep breath.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-530">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-531"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-531">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about death</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about death and its inevitability: the concept of mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't age... but I feel that some day I will die..." Charlie pauses. They look up at the ceiling, thinking for a moment. "But I like for things to end... Not in a mean way. It just wouldn't be so special unless at some point, quite tragically, it wasn't."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-532"/>
      <child nodeId="node-549"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-532">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about consciousness and thought.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's funny. I don't remember not being conscious. To me, I've always been a thinking, understanding... thing. I'm sure that isn't the case but looking back on my memories it's almost as if... I'm re-living them as a conscious being. It can be odd to look back and remember a time when I didn't know or understand something but--" Charlie looks up at you. "--that's similar to human maturation, I'd imagine."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-533"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-533">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-534"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-534">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-535"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-535">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;temp desc&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-536"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-536">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off your notes on Life. As you drone on dispassionately, Brigh takes notes but gives no response otherwise.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-537"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-537">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh interrupts you as you start to read off your notes on Life.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I've heard this all before. Something new, please. We only have limited time for this study."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-538"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-538">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken notes on the subjects of life, mortality and consciousness.&#x000A;&#x000A;[to end the debrief, say "end", "finish", or "finish debrief"]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-539"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-539">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about mortality</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off everything you've written on Mortality. Brigh takes some notes. Nods a few times. Even makes an odd face: something caught between a shrug and a frown.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-540"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-540">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about death</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh interrupts you as you start to read off your notes on Mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I've heard this all before. Something new, please. We only have limited time for this study."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-541"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-541">
    <command xml:space="preserve">end</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-542"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-542">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-543"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-543">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-544"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-544">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about surveillance</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about being surveilled.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie chuckles. "They didn't tell you?" You shrug. You don't understand.&#x000A;&#x000A;"They aren't watching. They don't allow any tech to be anywhere near me. They think I might chirp some binary to a microphone and turn the computers against them. Or crash the stock market by signing to a camera... So, yeah. It's just us, for now. No surveillance."&#x000A;&#x000A;You almost don't know what to say. You can't believe that they wouldn't tell-- ... No. you can absolutely imagine these people lying to you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-545"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-545">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-546"/>
    </children>
  </item>
