  <item nodeId="node-548">
    <command xml:space="preserve">brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Doctor Brigh or Doctor Brigh?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-549">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about freedom</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about freedom, you try to frame the discussion around the right itself, not Charlie's specific freedom.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was being transported to the facility, I was already at a stage where they feared plugging directly into me, for fear I might... I don't know-- escape? Take over?" Charlie waves their hands dismissively.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, they transported me in a sound-proof metal cube. Correct me if I'm wrong-- I don't believe that humans are transported in that way."&#x000A;&#x000A;3 questions asked!!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-550">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about mortality</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about death and its inevitability: the concept of mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't age... but I feel that some day I will die..." Charlie pauses. They look up at the ceiling, thinking for a moment. "But I like for things to end... Not in a mean way. It just wouldn't be so special unless at some point, quite tragically, it wasn't."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-551"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-551">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">If you didn't already know otherwise... you would never be able to tell that Charlie is not human. Their dark brown eyes flit back and forth between yours with instinctual humanity. Their skin looks soft and porous. As they wait for you to speak, they clasp their hands together in their lap as if to assure you of their patience. They cock their head to the side and sit up slightly in their chair. You almost laugh in astonishment. They are exquisite.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-552"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-552">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. They fidget slightly in their chair, adjusting for some apparent discomfort. You see a small, impermanent wince flit across their face. How fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-553"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-553">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about surveillanec</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about being surveilled.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie chuckles. "I don't mind. I wouldn't mind being watched for the rest of my life if it meant I could go and do something... real? I want to see the sun. I want to run in an open field. I want to work-- to have a job. I want to meet up with friends... I just-- I don't want to keep doing the same thing over and over and over again."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-554"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-554">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
