    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about self</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(myself)&#x000A;Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You read off everything you've written on myself. Brigh takes some notes. Nods a few times. Even makes an odd face: something caught between a shrug and a frown.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-574">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note.]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-575">
    <command xml:space="preserve">say hello to charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"Hello." You are able to muster, in a reasonably casual tone.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Hello!" says Charlie, a bit more excitedly than your nervous sputterings, "I hear you are going to ask me some questions. Please, ask away!"&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-576"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-576">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Charlie)&#x000A;You ask Charlie about... Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles wide. "I was hoping you were going to ask me that! I am an android, created with the intent of accurately simulating human consciousness. As far as I know, my creator successfully implemented a self-learning algorithm that got somewhat out of hand. Either I was given up or the government intervened... and I was moved here. That was 8 years 7 months and 14 days ago. Since then I have been kept in a small room, through that door." They gesture to a black door opposite the red door you came through. "At first they were running a bunch of tests on me but I think they got a bit scared at the rate I was developing."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-577"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-577">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about communism</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-578"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-578">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-579"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-579">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-580"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-580">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish debrief</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.&#x000A;&#x000A;DAY 1.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-581">
    <command xml:space="preserve">say hi to charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"Hello." You are able to muster, in a reasonably casual tone.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Hello!" says Charlie, a bit more excitedly than your nervous sputterings, "I hear you are going to ask me some questions. Please, ask away!"&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-582"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-582">
    <command xml:space="preserve">follow up on life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-583">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about discord</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-584"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-584">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
