  <item nodeId="node-615">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-616"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-616">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-617"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-617">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about mortality</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about death and its inevitability: the concept of mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't age... but I feel that some day I will die..." Charlie pauses. They look up at the ceiling, thinking for a moment. "But I like for things to end... Not in a mean way. It just wouldn't be so special unless at some point, quite tragically, it wasn't."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-618"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-618">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about computation</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-619"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-619">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about surveillance</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-620"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-620">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-621"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-621">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;temp desc&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-622"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-622">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You report on your notes on Life. Brigh scribbles away on his notebook, nodding intermittently.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-623"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-623">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about mortality</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You read off everything you've written on Mortality. Brigh takes some notes. Nods a few times. Even makes an odd face: something caught between a shrug and a frown.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-624"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-624">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about chaos</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">This provokes no reaction.&#x000A;&#x000A;[to end the debrief, say "end", "finish", or "finish debrief"]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-625"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-625">
    <command xml:space="preserve">end</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-626"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-626">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 3.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;The beginnings of the sun carve streaks across the horizon, rays of hope for the coming day. The morning is calm and warm. You close your eyes and take a deep breath.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-627"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-627">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The observation room seems quieter than usual when you enter today. Charlie sits calmly, they glance towards you as you enter before casually looking away. You can tell that they are trying to look blas&#x00E9; but they are practically bursting at the seams with excitement, even on day three.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-628"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-628">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">If you didn't already know otherwise... you would never be able to tell that Charlie is not human. Their dark brown eyes flit back and forth between yours with instinctual humanity. Their skin looks soft and porous. As they wait for you to speak, they clasp their hands together in their lap as if to assure you of their patience. They cock their head to the side and sit up slightly in their chair. You almost laugh in astonishment. They are exquisite.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-629"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-629">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. They are dressed in loose fitting, white-linen clothes, similar in silhouette to scrubs. As Charlie adjusts their position, they pull at the folds and creases of cloth that cling to their body in absentminded insecurity.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-630"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-630">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. Charlie picks at something on their hand, distracted by some manufactured impurity. You fight the urge to leap out of your chair at inspect their hand. You're already obsessing over what is emergent and what is pre-programmed.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-631">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about nothing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no, global safety."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-632"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-632">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You see nothing special about Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-633"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-633">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-634"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-634">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x Doctor Brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-635">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about north</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-636"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-636">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-637"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-637">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;You are seated across from Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well. Welcome to the facility. I hope that onboarding went smoothly." Onboarding? If being stripped of almost all of your belongings and then told not to do a laundry list of things is onboarding... you guess that happened. "My name is Elijah Brigh, you can call me Doctor Brigh. You've had your first session with the intelligence and during these debriefs you'll give me your insights and impressions. If you have any questions about procedures, feel free to ask. Otherwise, let's begin.&#x000A;&#x000A;"</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-638"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-638">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"Oh! And the input warning! I'm sure we told you." says Brigh, "It's all in the onboarding brief. You are not to tell it anything . It is a risk enough that it will learn through your questioning... Hell, it is likely learning just by interacting. The stoppage sensor is the only digital tech in the room and it is a closed system. So, if you tell it something the system will evacuate you. No exceptions.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-639">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about uhaul</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-640"/>
    </children>
  </item>
