    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-647">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;[7] tell brigh about charlie&#x000A;Which do you mean, Charlie or Themself?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] tell brigh about researchers&#x000A;Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You read off your notes on Researchers. Brigh takes notes silently.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-648"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-648">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Charlie or Themself?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-649"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-649">
    <command xml:space="preserve">charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Which do you mean, Charlie or Themself?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-650"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-650">
    <command xml:space="preserve">themself</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh about Charlie. You start to veer off rom your notes.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh sighs. "Remember: You are here to observe, not to socialize with the subject. We know that it is fascinating but it is also an unknown existential threat."&#x000A;&#x000A;You open your mouth to retort... but think better of it.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-651"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-651">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-652"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-652">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-653"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-653">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-654"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-654">
    <command xml:space="preserve"></command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I beg your pardon?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-655"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-655">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was younger-- when I could hear but not see --I thought that the world was dark for everyone. When my eyes were first installed it was like a different language. A loud, bright, incomprehensible mass of information. Once it finally solidified, I looked at my creator and saw she was speaking to me. I was so happy... But I was so happy for her... Because, I thought-- I'm so happy that you aren't in the dark anymore."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-656"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-656">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie to expand on their thoughts on growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie laughs. "I guess I didn't really answer the question, did I? It's not just that I've grown to understand that everyone else is living lives separate from me... I feel like I am finding my place in existence-- or where I want to be. My purpose.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-657"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-657">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie to continue expanding on the subject of growth.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Sometimes I imagine what it might be like to... To grow without the constraints of this facility." Charlie trails off, wringing their hands. "I think that would be nice. A good goal, I guess."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-658"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-658">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about growth again.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I think I've said enough about that..."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-659"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-659">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-660"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-660">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about death</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about death and its inevitability: the concept of mortality.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't age... but I feel that some day I will die..." Charlie pauses. They look up at the ceiling, thinking for a moment. "But I like for things to end... Not in a mean way. It just wouldn't be so special unless at some point, quite tragically, it wasn't."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-661"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-661">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Charlie)&#x000A;Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-662"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-662">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-663"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-663">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-664"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-664">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about growth</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You read off your notes on Growth. As you give your report you see Brigh suddenly straighten. For the remainder of the report he gives you his full attention, dilligently writing notes and nodding.&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-665">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">If you didn't already know otherwise... you would never be able to tell that Charlie is not human. Their dark brown eyes flit back and forth between yours with instinctual humanity. Their skin looks soft and porous. As they wait for you to speak, they clasp their hands together in their lap as if to assure you of their patience. They cock their head to the side and sit up slightly in their chair. You almost laugh in astonishment. They are exquisite.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-666"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-666">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. Their eyes are a dark brown, almost black. You lock eyes with them briefly and they glance away, seeming to feign self-consciousness. Perhaps it isn't an act?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-667"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-667">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. They fidget slightly in their chair, adjusting for some apparent discomfort. You see a small, impermanent wince flit across their face. How fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-668"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-668">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. They are dressed in loose fitting, white-linen clothes, similar in silhouette to scrubs. As Charlie adjusts their position, they pull at the folds and creases of cloth that cling to their body in absentminded insecurity.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-669"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-669">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look at Charlie again. They were manufactured to look organized and kempt but not perfect. Their nails are trimmed but have edges where they look to have been cut... Could their nails truly grow?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-670"/>
    </children>
  </item>
