  <item nodeId="node-733">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-734"/>
      <child nodeId="node-735"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-734">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Briefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "tell brigh about something". when you are done: "finish debrief".]&#x000A;3 questions asked!!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] tell charlie about jesus&#x000A;You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-735">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well. Welcome to the facility. I hope that onboarding went smoothly." Onboarding? If being stripped of almost all of your belongings and then told not to do a bunch of things then... you guess that happened. "My name is Elijah Brigh, you can call me Doctor Brigh. During these debriefs you'll give me your insights and impressions on the intelligencec. If you have any questions about procedures, feel free to ask. Otherwise, let's begin."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-736"/>
      <child nodeId="node-740"/>
      <child nodeId="node-741"/>
      <child nodeId="node-778"/>
      <child nodeId="node-781"/>
      <child nodeId="node-790"/>
      <child nodeId="node-794"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-736">
    <command xml:space="preserve"></command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I beg your pardon?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-737"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-737">
    <command xml:space="preserve">finish debrief</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Brigh raises his eyebrows. "You have to give me something. Why else would you be here?"&#x000A;&#x000A;You look down at your notepad. You flip through the pages. You've got some notes here, might as well share something with Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-738"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-738">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh nothing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no: global safety."</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-739"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-739">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.&#x000A;&#x000A;DAY 1.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-740">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> finish debrief</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A; The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.&#x000A;&#x000A;DAY 1.&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;temp desc</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-741">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[use "tell brigh about a noted topic" or you can "ask brigh about procedure" for more info].&#x000A;[when you are done, you can end the debrief with "end", "finish" or "finish debrief".]&#x000A;&gt;[7] tell brigh about charlie&#x000A;Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You tell Brigh about Charlie. You start to veer off from your notes.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh sighs. "Remember: You are here to observe, not to socialize with the subject. We know that it is fascinating but it is also an unknown existential threat."&#x000A;&#x000A;You open your mouth to retort... but think better of it.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] tell brigh about researchers&#x000A;You read off your notes on the researchers. As you drone on dispassionately, Brigh takes notes but gives no response otherwise.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[9] finish&#x000A;"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A;The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-742"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-742">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">DAY 2.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;A brisk breeze presses your coat against your body. You feel a pang of anxiety as you check your coat pockets. Your notepad is being kept at the facility for the duration of the study. Being without your notepad feels like being without a limb.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-743"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-743">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the distance you see the ominous cloud of your entourage. The start of another day.&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The metal gate to the observation room closes behind you with a hiss. Charlie is sitting at attention, looking towards you excitedly. They quietly watch you cross the room and sit across from them. You pull out your notebook, relishing in the familiarity of the paper as you flip to a blank page. You look up at Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[10] ask charlie about growth&#x000A;Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;"When I was younger-- when I could hear but not see --I thought that the world was dark for everyone. When my eyes were first installed it was like a different language. A loud, bright, incomprehensible mass of information. Once it finally solidified, I looked at my creator and saw she was speaking to me. I was so happy... But I was so happy for her... Because, I thought-- I'm so happy that you aren't in the dark anymore."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[11] ask charlie about growth&#x000A;You ask Charlie to expand on their thoughts on growth and development.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie laughs. "I guess I didn't really answer the question, did I? It's not just that I've grown to understand that everyone else is living lives separate from me... I feel like I am finding my place in existence-- or where I want to be. My purpose.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[12] ask charlie about surveillance&#x000A;You ask Charlie about being surveilled.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie chuckles. "They didn't tell you?" You shrug. You don't understand.&#x000A;&#x000A;"They aren't watching. They don't allow any tech to be anywhere near me. They think I might chirp some binary to a microphone and turn the computers against them. Or crash the stock market by signing to a camera... So, yeah. It's just us, for now. No surveillance."&#x000A;&#x000A;You almost don't know what to say. You can't believe that they wouldn't tell-- ... No. you can absolutely imagine these people lying to you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[13] ask charlie about freedom&#x000A;Before you can get out your question the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-744"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-744">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous buzzing sound, the room is suddenly filled with a sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"INPUT LIMIT REACHED. INPUT LIMIT REACHED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh. You stand up and look down at Charlie. They smile sadly and say, "See you tomorrow."&#x000A;&#x000A;You return a smile, though it may have come out as more of a pitiful grimace. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-745"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-745">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Debriefing Room&#x000A;You're back in the odd, uncomfortable debrief room.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across the metal table sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[14] tell brigh about nothing&#x000A;Brigh looks relieved that you skip the pleasantries.&#x000A;&#x000A;You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no: global safety."</result>
