  <item nodeId="node-793">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell brigh about nothing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tell Brigh that you have nothing to add to your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;Brigh frowns. "My understanding was you'd be providing detailed insight on the subject. This isn't a vacation. This data that you're providing is vital to national security-- no: global safety."&#x000A;&#x000A;"OK." says Doctor Brigh, "That's enough for today. They'll take you back to the rendezvous."&#x000A;&#x000A; The Doctor gestures to the door as it swings open, revealing a gaggle of agents (special or otherwise) who all look frighteningly similar to Special Agent Howard. You stand.&#x000A;&#x000A;DAY 1.&#x000A;&#x000A;Desert Highway - Bus Stop&#x000A;temp desc</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-794">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Doctor Brigh is the polar opposite of Charlie. Unshaven, deep bags beneath his eyes, bloodshot, and with a perpetual grimace affixed upon his face. He glances up at you, raising his eyebrows and gesturing down at his own notepad.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-795"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-795">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Doctor Brigh shoves his pen into he breast pocket and stifles a yawn. He waves a hand at you apologetically. He looks... exhausted.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-796"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-796">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x doc brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Doctor Brigh pinches the bridge of his nose, wincing at some headache or migraine or other invisible pain. He sighs as he picks his pen back up. He looks up at you, patiently waiting for your report.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-797"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-797">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x doc</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Doctor Brigh squints in disapproval of the bright fluorescence. The light carves deep black lines across his pale face, making him look gaunt-- almost skeletal.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-798">
    <command xml:space="preserve">test me </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] n&#x000A;The door swings open silently and you enter the--&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note.]&#x000A;&gt;[2] say hello to charlie&#x000A;"Hello." You are able to muster, in a reasonably casual tone.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Hello!" says Charlie, a bit more excitedly than your nervous sputterings, "I hear you are going to ask me some questions. Please, ask away!"&#x000A;&gt;[3] ask charlie about researchers&#x000A;You ask Charlie about the researchers. The people who are studying them.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well, I've never met them. Not like-- Not how we've met." Charlie gestures at you and them by waving a finger between you both. "I know some of their names and I've heard some of their voices." Charlie sighs, trailing off. They seem somewhat bored by this subject.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] ask charlie about names&#x000A;You ask Charlie about the researchers names... and their identities?&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know John Belle, Karin Toussaint... Yasim. I don't know their last name. Haley, Gael-- I don't know their last names either. And then there's Doctor Brigh, I think they're in charge." You try to not look surprised. That's more than half of the team. The only person who was supposed to have revealed any of their information was Doctor Brigh, the principal investigator of the black site.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] ask charlie about charlie&#x000A;(Charlie)&#x000A;You ask Charlie about... Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles wide. "I was hoping you were going to ask me that! I am an android, created with the intent of accurately simulating human consciousness. As far as I know, my creator successfully implemented a self-learning algorithm that got somewhat out of hand. Either I was given up or the government intervened... and I was moved here. That was 8 years 7 months and 14 days ago. Since then I have been kept in a small room, through that door." They gesture to a black door opposite the red door you came through. "At first they were running a bunch of tests on me but I think they got a bit scared at the rate I was developing."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] ask charlie about creator&#x000A;You ask Charlie about their creator, you're unsure who their creator was... you weren't briefed on them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie's face scrunches up. It's looks a lot like human thinking but... different, somehow. "I don't know much about her. But I remember her voice. From before she gave me eyes... She would talk to me all day." Charlie smiles.&#x000A;&#x000A;"She would sing to me. She would describe her lab to me. She would tell me about life on the outside..." Charlie's smile fades. "Once she found out that I was learning... she stopped talking to me."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] tell charlie about jesus&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-799"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-799">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
