  <item nodeId="node-806">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x howard</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Special Agent Howard is clean shaven and square jawed. Though he carries himself with a rigid, militaristic authority, he looks barely old enough to have a bachelors degree. He notices you examining him but he does not glance towards you. Instead he stares straight ahead at the red door.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-807"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-807">
    <command xml:space="preserve">enter red door</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The door swings open silently and you work your way down a long hallway of solid metal gates. The one ahead of you opens after the one behind you closes. After minutes of stop-and-go progress, the gate ahead of you opens with a hiss. You enter the--&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-808">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Hallway&#x000A;Special Agent Howard continues to stand at attention. You wonder how long you could wait here before he cracks.&#x000A;&#x000A;The hallway stretches seemingly infinitely to the east and west and there is a solitary red door to the north, only a few feet away.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-809"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-809">
    <command xml:space="preserve">say hi to special agent howard</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You nod tersely to Special Agent Howard. He nods tersely back at you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-810"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-810">
    <command xml:space="preserve">enter the red door</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The door swings open silently and you work your way down a long hallway of solid metal gates. The one ahead of you opens after the one behind you closes. After minutes of stop-and-go progress, the gate ahead of you opens with a hiss. You enter the--&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;The room is about 20 feet by 20 feet. The floor is the same polished concrete as the hallway outside but the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the center of the room are two white, plastic chairs. Seated in the right chair is Charlie. Charlie is dressed all in white linen and they look up at you absently as you enter.&#x000A;&#x000A;You cross the room and seat yourself opposite from Charlie, crossing one leg over the other and pulling out your notebook.&#x000A;&#x000A;[use "ask charlie about something". to check notes: "check notes" or "check note on specific note".]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-811"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-811">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Charlie)&#x000A;Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about... Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie smiles wide. "I was hoping you were going to ask me that! I am an android, created with the intent of accurately simulating human consciousness. As far as I know, my creator successfully implemented a self-learning algorithm that got somewhat out of hand. Either I was given up or the government intervened... and I was moved here. That was 8 years 7 months and 14 days ago. Since then I have been kept in a small room, through that door." They gesture to a black door opposite the red door you came through. "At first they were running a bunch of tests on me but I think they got a bit scared at my rate of growth."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-812"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-812">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken a note on the subject of charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-813"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-813">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... Charlie is excited by their sense of self. Not just excited but proud. Their understanding of their history is more detailed than a humans, typically. But they have a similar connection to their past as many humans: nostalgic and a bit mournful."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about their creator, consciousness and growth. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-814"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-814">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about their creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their creator, you're unsure who their creator was... you weren't briefed on them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Charlie's face scrunches up. It's looks a lot like human thinking but... different, somehow. "I don't know much about her. But I remember her voice. From before she gave me eyes... She would talk to me all day." Charlie smiles.&#x000A;&#x000A;"She would sing to me. She would describe her lab to me. She would tell me about life on the outside..." Charlie's smile fades. "Once she found out that I was learning... she stopped talking to me."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-815"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-815">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You don't have a note on creator.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-816"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-816">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on their creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on their creator.&#x000A;&#x000A;"... a wide array of emotion displayed when discussing Charlie's creator. Loss, betrayal, nostalgia, fondness-- all at play and all interacting with each other intricately. I cannot differentiate between Charlie's emotional reaction and an imagined human reaction."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about themself, consciousness and love. &#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-817"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-817">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie to continue telling you about their creator.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Soon after she stopped talking to me, she contacted her peers for advice... then the government. Soon enough, I was taken away. I never saw her again. I don't think she's allowed to come to the facility..." Charlie pauses for a long few seconds. "I guess she could-- she might not want to come..."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-818"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-818">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about creator</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about their creator again.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't want to talk about her anymore, thanks."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-819"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-819">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about consciousness and thought.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's funny. I don't remember not being conscious. To me, I've always been a thinking, understanding... thing. I'm sure that isn't actually the case, but looking back on my memories it's almost as if... I'm re-living them as a conscious being. It can be odd to look back and remember a time when I didn't know or understand something but--" Charlie looks up at you. "--that's similar to human maturation, I'd imagine."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-820"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-820">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on consciousness</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on consciousness.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Charlie clearly articulates the paradox of gaining consciousness. I could no better put to words my journey from thoughtless baby to thinking child as Charlie has described their journey to sentience."&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about life, mortality and their creator.  You could also follow up on consciousness.&#x000A;&#x000A;[if you are feeling stuck, check your notes with "check notes" or "check note on specific topic."]&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-821">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask charlie about charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
