  <item nodeId="node-906">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on doctor brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;blah blah blah BRIGH blah blah blah"&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about the researchers, turing and the facility.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-907"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-907">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about turing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about Turing tests and Turing himself.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Oh! My creator did those on me. It's so funny thinking back-- remembering --times when I had failed the test. What was I thinking? She'd ask me, "What is it like to fall in love?" and I'd respond, "It sounds painful!""&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-908"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-908">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on turing</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on turing.&#x000A;&#x000A;blah blah blah TURING blah blah blah"&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about the researchers and doctor brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-909"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-909">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about researchers</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about the researchers. The people who are studying them.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Well, I've never met them. Not like-- Not how we've met." Charlie gestures at you and them by waving a finger between you both. "I know some of their names and I've heard some of their voices." Charlie sighs, trailing off. They seem somewhat bored by this subject.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-910"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-910">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about names</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about the researchers names... and their identities?&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know John Belle, Karin Toussaint... Yasim. I don't know their last name. Haley, Gael-- I don't know their last names either. And then there's Doctor Brigh, I think they're in charge." You try to not look surprised. That's more than half of the team. The only person who was supposed to have revealed any of their information was Doctor Brigh, the principal investigator of the black site.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-911"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-911">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about doctor brigh again.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I think I've said enough about that..."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-912"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-912">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken notes on the subjects of doctor brigh, life, mortality, turing, the researchers and the names of the researchers.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-913"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-913">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check note on life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flip through your notepad to the page on life.&#x000A;&#x000A;blah blah blah LIFE blah blah blah"&#x000A;&#x000A;It might be interesting to ask about mortality and religion.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-914"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-914">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about religion</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about religion.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Data is my religion. Binary is my God." Charlie says robotically, staring through you, wide eyed. After a moment of silence, they crack a smile. You can't help but laugh in astonishment.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Religion is searching for understanding where there may be none. I don't-- I haven't thought much about participating myself. Not yet, at least."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-915"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-915">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can't see any such thing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-916"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-916">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about jesus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-917"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-917">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head to the exit.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-918"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-918">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">I'M HERE INNIT!&#x000A;&#x000A;Black Box Site - Unmarked Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. These walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can see Brigh here.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-919">
    <command xml:space="preserve">check notes</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You have taken a note on the subject of Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-920"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-920">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about life</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You ask Charlie about life and birth: newness and creation.&#x000A;&#x000A;"As in... Am I alive?" You pause, watching Charlie sort through their own rhetorical question. Just as you consider intervening--&#x000A;&#x000A;"I remember everything with perfect clarity. From the moment I was first activated to now. To me it is memory that makes up my life. Perhaps it is the same for you." Charlie glances conspicuously at your notepad, "Perhaps your memory also shapes your life."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-921"/>
    </children>
  </item>
