  <item nodeId="node-931">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ask about doctor brigh</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(addressing Charlie)&#x000A;Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;You ask Charlie about Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know that they are the principal investigator in this facility... I still remember the first thing they said to me--" Charlie puts on a faux frown and speaks in a gruff voice. "No Turings for you Charlie. I know you'd pass. No point in doin" that." The impression takes you so by surprise that you can't help but laugh. It's actually quite a good impression. You're sure that Charlie would be capable of perfectly recreating the Doctor's voice... but they elected instead to create a caricatured, flawed impersonation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-932"/>
    </children>
  </item>
