"&#x000A;    block swinging rule response (A): "[There's] nothing sensible to swing here."&#x000A;    can't rub another person rule response (A): "[The noun] [might not like] that."&#x000A;    report rubbing rule response (A): "[We] [rub] [the noun]."&#x000A;    report rubbing rule response (B): "[The actor] [rub] [the noun]."&#x000A;    block setting it to rule response (A): "No, [we] [can't set] [regarding the noun][those] to anything."&#x000A;    report waving hands rule response (A): "[We] [wave]."&#x000A;    report waving hands rule response (B): "[The actor] [wave]."&#x000A;    block buying rule response (A): "Nothing [are] on sale."&#x000A;    block climbing rule response (A): "Little [are] to be achieved by that."&#x000A;    block sleeping rule response (A): "[We] [aren't] feeling especially drowsy."&#x000A;Basic Screen Effects by Emily Short:&#x000A;    standard pausing the game rule response (A): "[paragraph break]Please press SPACE to continue."&#x000A;Conversation Framework by Eric Eve:&#x000A;    block informing rule response (A): "[There] [are] no reply."&#x000A;    block quizzing rule response (A): "Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. 'Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet.'"&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (A): "[There's] no one [here] to talk to."&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (B): "You need to specify who you want to speak to."&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (C): "(addressing [the interlocutor])"&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (D): "[We] [aren't] talking to anyone."&#x000A;    can't converse with absent interlocutor rule response (A): "[The current interlocutor] [aren't] [here]."&#x000A;    can't greet current interlocutor rule response (A): "Talking to [ourselves] [regarding nothing][are] unrewarding."&#x000A;    can't greet current interlocutor rule response (B): "[We] [are] already talking to [the noun]."&#x000A;    can't greet yourself rule response (A): "Talking to [ourselves] [regarding nothing][are] likely to prove unrewarding."&#x000A;    default greeting rule response (A): "[We] [say] hello to [the noun]."&#x000A;    check what's being hailed rule response (A): "[We] [are] already talking to [the current interlocutor]."&#x000A;    check what's being hailed rule response (B): "(addressing [the noun])"&#x000A;    can't say goodbye to someone you're not talking to rule response (A): "[We] [aren't] talking to [the noun]."&#x000A;    don't allow saying goodbye to no-one rule response (A): "[We] [aren't] talking to anyone."&#x000A;Epistemology by Eric Eve:&#x000A;    report epistemic status rule response (A): "[noun] - [if the noun is seen]seen[otherwise]unseen[end if] /&#x000A;[if the noun is familiar]familiar[otherwise]unfamiliar[end if] /&#x000A;[if the noun is known]known[otherwise]unknown[end if]."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
