  <item nodeId="node-1088">
    <command xml:space="preserve">responses</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">&gt;--&gt; The following sets of responses are available:&#x000A;    RESPONSES ALL&#x000A;    RESPONSES 1: Standard Rules&#x000A;    RESPONSES 2: Basic Screen Effects by Emily Short&#x000A;    RESPONSES 3: Conversation Framework by Eric Eve&#x000A;    RESPONSES 4: Epistemology by Eric Eve&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1089"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1089">
    <command xml:space="preserve">3</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">That's not a verb I recognise.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1090"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1090">
    <command xml:space="preserve">RESPONSES 3</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Conversation Framework by Eric Eve:&#x000A;    block informing rule response (A): "[There] [are] no reply."&#x000A;    block quizzing rule response (A): "Charlie's face scrunches up in discomfort. 'Sorry... I don't know anything about that... Not yet.'"&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (A): "[There's] no one [here] to talk to."&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (B): "You need to specify who you want to speak to."&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (C): "(addressing [the interlocutor])"&#x000A;    implicit-conversing needs current interlocutor rule response (D): "[We] [aren't] talking to anyone."&#x000A;    can't converse with absent interlocutor rule response (A): "[The current interlocutor] [aren't] [here]."&#x000A;    can't greet current interlocutor rule response (A): "Talking to [ourselves] [regarding nothing][are] unrewarding."&#x000A;    can't greet current interlocutor rule response (B): "[We] [are] already talking to [the noun]."&#x000A;    can't greet yourself rule response (A): "Talking to [ourselves] [regarding nothing][are] likely to prove unrewarding."&#x000A;    default greeting rule response (A): "[We] [say] hello to [the noun]."&#x000A;    check what's being hailed rule response (A): "[We] [are] already talking to [the current interlocutor]."&#x000A;    check what's being hailed rule response (B): "(addressing [the noun])"&#x000A;    can't say goodbye to someone you're not talking to rule response (A): "[We] [aren't] talking to [the noun]."&#x000A;    don't allow saying goodbye to no-one rule response (A): "[We] [aren't] talking to anyone."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1091"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1091">
    <command xml:space="preserve">RESPONSES 4</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Epistemology by Eric Eve:&#x000A;    report epistemic status rule response (A): "[noun] - [if the noun is seen]seen[otherwise]unseen[end if] /&#x000A;[if the noun is familiar]familiar[otherwise]unfamiliar[end if] /&#x000A;[if the noun is known]known[otherwise]unknown[end if]."&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1092">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell charlie about utsfl</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie looks momentarily surprised as you speak before greeting them.&#x000A;&#x000A;Before you can get out the first half of a sentence the room darkens to near pitch black.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1093"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1093">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">BRRRRMM! --with an ominous, booming, buzzing sound; the room is suddenly filled with sinister red light.&#x000A;&#x000A;"ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ERRANT OUTPUT DETECTED. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER. ALL HUMANS EVACUATE THE OBSERVATION CHAMBER."&#x000A;&#x000A;You wince as the loud robotic voice encourages you to evacuate. You stand and look down at Charlie. They shrug but they don't get out of their chair. You head out the way you came.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1094"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1094">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Unmarked Room&#x000A;You sit in an uncomfortable chair. The room is non-descript, similar to the observation room but without the cushioned walls. The walls are instead made of glass and metal, making every sound reverberant and tinny.&#x000A;&#x000A;Across an empty metal table in front of you sits Doctor Brigh.&#x000A;&#x000A;Shit! You haven't taken any notes... You'll have to comee clean with Doctor Brigh and tell him nothing.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1095">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">If you didn't already know otherwise... you would never be able to tell that Charlie is not human. Their dark brown eyes flit back and forth between yours with instinctual humanity. Their skin looks soft and porous. As they wait for you to speak, they clasp their hands together in their lap as if to assure you of their patience. They cock their head to the side and sit up slightly in their chair. You almost laugh in astonishment. They are exquisite.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1096"/>
      <child nodeId="node-1097"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1096">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Black Box Site - Observation Room&#x000A;You glance around the room. The floor is polished concrete and the walls are padded with some sort of white cushioning. Seated across from you is Charlie.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1097">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Charlie Desc 2&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1098"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-1098">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x charlie</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You look over Charlie again. They were manufactured to look organized and kempt but not perfect. Their nails are trimmed but have edges where they look to have been cut... Could they have growing nails?&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-1099"/>
    </children>
  </item>
